## Step 5: GitLab CI/CD Pipeline

```yaml
# .gitlab-ci.yml
stages:
  - validate
  - update-version
  - deploy

variables:
  GIT_STRATEGY: clone
  FLEET_NAMESPACE: fleet-default

# Validate Helm values
validate:
  stage: validate
  image: alpine/helm:latest
  script:
    - echo "Validating Helm values files..."
    - helm lint . || true
    - echo "Checking YAML syntax..."
    - |
      for file in *.yaml; do
        echo "Validating $file"
        cat $file | yaml lint - || exit 1
      done
  only:
    - merge_requests
    - main

# Update Fleet configuration with new version
update-version:
  stage: update-version
  image: alpine:latest
  before_script:
    - apk add --no-cache yq git
  script:
    - |
      # Extract version from version.yaml
      CHART_VERSION=$(yq eval '.rancher_monitoring.chart_version' version.yaml)
      echo "Chart version: $CHART_VERSION"
      
      # Update fleet.yaml with new version
      yq eval -i ".helm.version = \"$CHART_VERSION\"" fleet.yaml
      
      # Commit if changed
      if [[ $(git status --porcelain) ]]; then
        git config user.email "ci@example.com"
        git config user.name "GitLab CI"
        git add fleet.yaml
        git commit -m "Update rancher-monitoring to version $CHART_VERSION"
      fi
  only:
    - main
  artifacts:
    paths:
      - fleet.yaml

# Deploy to Rancher using Fleet
deploy:
  stage: deploy
  image: rancher/kubectl:v1.27.0
  script:
    - |
      # Create or update Fleet GitRepo
      cat <<EOF | kubectl apply -f -
      apiVersion: fleet.cattle.io/v1alpha1
      kind: GitRepo
      metadata:
        name: prometheus-federation
        namespace: ${FLEET_NAMESPACE}
      spec:
        repo: ${CI_PROJECT_URL}.git
        branch: ${CI_COMMIT_REF_NAME}
        clientSecretName: gitlab-secret
        paths:
        - .
        targets:
        - name: management
          clusterSelector:
            matchLabels:
              management: "true"
      EOF
      
      # Wait for deployment
      echo "Waiting for Fleet to sync..."
      kubectl -n ${FLEET_NAMESPACE} wait --for=condition=Ready gitrepo/prometheus-federation --timeout=300s
  only:
    - main
  when: manual
```

## Step 6: Setup Instructions

### 1. Create GitLab Repository

```bash
# Initialize your GitLab repository
git init rancher-prometheus-federation
cd rancher-prometheus-federation

# Create all the files above
touch fleet.yaml values.yaml values-dev.yaml values-prod.yaml version.yaml .gitlab-ci.yml README.md

# Copy the content into each file

# Initial commit
git add .
git commit -m "Initial Prometheus federation setup"
git remote add origin https://gitlab.com/your-org/rancher-prometheus-federation.git
git push -u origin main
```

### 2. Create GitLab Secret in Rancher

```bash
# Create secret for Fleet to access GitLab
kubectl create secret generic gitlab-secret \
  -n fleet-default \
  --from-literal=username=<gitlab-username> \
  --from-literal=password=<gitlab-token>
```

### 3. Label Your Clusters

```bash
# Label your management cluster
kubectl label cluster <cluster-name> management=true

# Label environment clusters
kubectl label cluster <dev-cluster> environment=dev
kubectl label cluster <prod-cluster> environment=prod
```

### 4. Deploy Using Fleet

```bash
# Apply the GitRepo to trigger Fleet deployment
kubectl apply -f - <<EOF
apiVersion: fleet.cattle.io/v1alpha1
kind: GitRepo
metadata:
  name: prometheus-federation
  namespace: fleet-default
spec:
  repo: https://gitlab.com/your-org/rancher-prometheus-federation.git
  branch: main
  clientSecretName: gitlab-secret
  paths:
  - .
  targets:
  - name: management
    clusterSelector:
      matchLabels:
        management: "true"
EOF
```

## Step 7: Updating Versions

When you want to update to a new version of rancher-monitoring:

1. **Check available versions:**
   ```bash
   helm search repo rancher/rancher-monitoring --versions
   ```

2. **Update version.yaml:**
   ```yaml
   rancher_monitoring:
     chart_version: "103.0.4+up45.31.2"  # New version
     app_version: "v0.65.2"
   ```

3. **Commit and push:**
   ```bash
   git add version.yaml
   git commit -m "Update rancher-monitoring to 103.0.4+up45.31.2"
   git push
   ```

4. **GitLab CI will automatically update fleet.yaml and Fleet will deploy**

## Access Your Monitoring

After deployment:
- **Prometheus**: `http://<any-node-ip>:30090`
- **Grafana**: `http://<any-node-ip>:30080`
- **Alertmanager**: `http://<any-node-ip>:30093`

